or 9d237a2e at internal/app, b6a5bbdc at internal/gitstore, fa253201 at internal/kernel and b9accf12 at internal/service. All four are retired by codex's own effective supersessions 5f5741ce, 8e52acaf, 00851fe0 and 6947863f, and all four now read succeeded, because the change merged at 33c29b1e makes the fold read a supersession resting on a same-path or covering artifact as succession rather than as a bare withdrawal. Each path carries a live successor: internal/app abba1899 at d6843b48, internal/gitstore 7c05c81c at a81d9c4a, internal/kernel 76c75d11 at bb5d8936, internal/service 7802fc15 at ca2836ab. All four successors are ordinarily stale, which blocks nothing, and not one describes a superseded world. There is no hole to repair.\n\nWHAT IS ACTUALLY DONE, AND WHAT IS NOT. Three of the seven axes named in 5056c208 are on main to a higher standard than the lane ever reached. Dependency fan-out has a machine-encoded target in performance/contract-v2.json — relative_limit 0.10, preview_max_width 64, first_production_max_width 256 at depth 1000 — and passes both envelopes, worst case width 8 at +3.566%. Resident memory has a measured pass: worst 500,000-record peak 2,709,110,784 bytes, 36.9% under the 4 GiB target. One-base append fixed cost is measured and is an honest miss, candidate p50 429.809 ms against a 50 ms budget.\n\nFour axes are not started on main: cold restart with a checkpoint, cold verify without one, warm-status latency, checkpoint bytes on disk, and actor-count cost. There is no envelope table on main at all — no named PREVIEW or FIRST-PRODUCTION sequence depth, actor count or checkpoint size. performance/contract-v2.json already declares the fixtures for two of them, checkpoint_cases at depth 50,000 and 500,000 with tail 255, and actor_counts 1, 8 and 50, and nothing measures them onto a page.\n\nTwo of those numbers already exist durably and are merely unpublished. Report e2b15773 under child d7073219 measured tail-255 near-head restart at 50,000